('A0016', NULL, 'Weaving Pandan Mats', 'Education Tourism', 0, '<p>Weaving Pandan Mats</p>', '1700128166_6b511894fc7df4120f7d.mp4', 0x0000000001060000000100000001030000000100000004000000919b63bc750c59403db1753ff2b8e6bf2a973cf6750c5940aae3612b0fb9e6bf8a71bfb2750c59409a965efd13b9e6bf919b63bc750c59403db1753ff2b8e6bf, 0x0000000001060000000100000001030000000100000004000000919b63bc750c59403db1753ff2b8e6bf2a973cf6750c5940aae3612b0fb9e6bf8a71bfb2750c59409a965efd13b9e6bf919b63bc750c59403db1753ff2b8e6bf, 1),
('A0017', 'GTP01', 'Fisherman\'s Friend', 'Education Tourism', 0, '<p>When visiting Ulakan GTP, visitors will be able to enjoy the natural beauty of the coast. This tour is unique in its beach conditions. Where there are sandbars that limit direct beach interaction with sea water, called estuary.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Estuary</strong>, derived from the Latin word <em>&quot;aestus&quot;</em> meaning tides, represents the confluence of fresh water and sea water. Its definition encapsulates its primary characteristic as a semi-enclosed water mass in coastal areas directly connected to the open sea. Influenced by tidal effects, estuaries transform into water masses that blend seawater and freshwater.</p>\r\n<p>In the tourist village of Green Talao Park, the prevalent type of estuary is a semi-closed bay or Gobah, formed by sand dunes parallel to the coastline, hindering direct interaction with seawater.</p>\r\n<p>The majority of estuaries are characterized by muddy substrates, deposits transported by both fresh and marine water. Encompassing river mouths, bays, and tidal swamps, estuaries are recognized as ecotones&mdash;zones where two distinct ecosystems (freshwater and marine) converge, giving rise to habitats with unique characteristics. The diverse habitats contribute to the richness of aquatic resources, with fish fauna playing a central role.</p>', 'tracking.mp4', , , 1);

